hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2995","**\nNarrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi, who said: Narrated to us Waki', who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, who said: Narrated to us 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of his father, who said:\n\"I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) at al-Abtah, and he was in a red tent. Bilal (RA) then came out with the leftover water from his ablution. Between those who took some of it to drink and those who collected it, Bilal (RA) gave the call to prayer. I would follow his mouth like this and like this,\" meaning to the right and left.\nHe (RA) said: \"Then a spear was planted for him, and the Prophet (ﷺ) came out wearing a red cloak or a red garment. I can still see the gleam of his shins. He prayed two rak'ahs towards the spear for Zuhr or 'Asr. A woman, a donkey, and a dog would pass in front of him, but it did not prevent him from praying. He continued to pray two rak'ahs until he reached al-Madinah.\"\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) said: \"I have compiled the various chains of the report of Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas (RA), in another place.\""
"2996","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abdah, who said: 'Abd al-Warith informed us, from Yahya (and he is Ibn Abi Ishaq), from Anas ibn Malik (RA), who said:\n\"We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from al-Madinah to Makkah, and he would pray two rak'ahs with us until we returned to al-Madinah.\"\nI said to him: \"Did you stay in Makkah for anything?\"\nHe said: \"We stayed there for ten (days).\"\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
